{
  "scenario": "A digital forensics lab acquires the laptop and phone of an engineer suspected of leaking a company's gearbox designs. FTK Imager, behind a write blocker, images the laptop's disk, and UFED extracts the phone; Autopsy then finds a ZIP archive of the designs, the email that sent it to a personal address, a file-sharing upload page and an SMS about it. Each acquisition and analysis records its performer, instruments, inputs and results, observables carry their properties in facets, and hashes and containment relationships tie them together.",
